<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nellore</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nellore is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andhra-pradesh">Andhra Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, on the Penna river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-bengal">Bay of Bengal</a> coast. In the 12th and 13th centuries it was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telugu-cholas">Telugu Chodas</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jatavarman-sundara-pandya-i">Jatavarman Sundara Pandya I</a> performed a victory coronation there. It later came under the Kakatiyas and Vijayanagara and is now a district headquarters.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nellore.jpg" alt="Nellore" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: YVSREDDY · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sri_Ranganathaswamy_Temple,_Galigopuram,_Nellore_(4).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
